abstract: >
  SIRIUS LOCAL AI is a fully modular, offline-only AI runtime designed for secure,
  deterministic execution of commands, workflows, plugins, and semantic automation.
  Version 5.3.0 introduces major stability improvements, including the ENVOY Execution
  Layer 5, ENVOY Permission Layer 5, optimized Workflow Engine 5.3, stabilized Knowledge
  Graph 5.x modules, and improved multimodal triage through AITE 5.3.

  The Unified Runtime Architecture 5.x merges PC and Mobile logic into a single,
  deterministic, identity-aware operating layer. The Runtime Core 5.3 provides unified
  orchestration, deterministic execution, capability-based access control, and identity-
  aware routing across all modules.

  SECURITY FAMILY 5.x expands identity and family safety layers with OWNER/FAMILY/
  STRANGER identity levels, time-limits v3, safe-mode for unknown users, and a
  Schoolwork Engine ensuring unrestricted access to academic tasks.

  The system operates entirely on the user's device, without any cloud dependencies
  or external data transmission. All modules follow strict security boundaries,
  deterministic behavior, semantic understanding, and predictable execution rules.

  Version 5.3.0 upgrades the entire runtime stack, including Workflow Engine 5.3,
  Reasoning Engine 5.0, ENVOY 5, FS‑AGENT 5, CME‑MEM 5, System Agent 5, and Password
  Vault 5.0. These upgrades prepare the architecture for the upcoming Self‑Repair
  Layer in the 5.x → 6.0 transition.
